                <pb facs="0178" n="76" sameAs="frus:frus1927v03/pg76"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">838.00/2406: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The High Commissioner in Haiti</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Russell</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Port au Prince</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1927-10-05T11:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">October 5,
                                1927—11 a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 2:35
                    p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>135. President Borno this morning sent for me and stated that a number of members
                    of Council of State representing a majority had just called on him and desired
                    to change paragraph 1 of article 72 to read that the term of office of President
                    shall last for 6 years, this in order to give him (President Borno) two more
                    years. I informed him that I could not agree to such a radical change without
                    first obtaining approval of the Department. The President stated that there was
                    not time for that as the amendments must be voted today and that he would
                    consequently request the Council not to make the change it desires.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Russell</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
